Compendium Registry — License Split
===================================

This repository contains two kinds of work, licensed separately:

1. JSON manifest files — public-domain dedication (CC0 1.0 Universal)
   --------------------------------------------------------------------
   index.json
   languages/*.json
   tools/*.json

   Use, copy, modify, and distribute without restriction or attribution.
   Full text: see LICENSE.data (or
   https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode)

2. Source code — MIT License
   ---------------------------
   Python scripts (build_manifest_split.py, package_tools.py,
   fetch_checksums.py, etc.), shell helpers, and any other code in this
   repository.

   Full text: see LICENSE.code (or https://opensource.org/license/mit/)

Files not explicitly covered above (e.g. README.md) fall under the source-
code license (MIT).

This split lets the data be reused freely (no attribution friction for
package managers, mirrors, or tooling that depends on the manifests) while
keeping the code under a permissive but attribution-bearing license.
